1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,328
Narrator: Scenario 18. Infrastructure operations.

2
00:00:05,928 --> 00:00:18,072
A: A physical disk has failed in the production storage array. The service remains available, but redundancy is reduced. The hardware alert needs prompt attention.

3
00:00:18,672 --> 00:00:27,528
B: We have a replacement available in the data center. Do you want us to replace the disk now, or should we wait for further checks?

4
00:00:28,128 --> 00:00:40,320
C: Please wait until we confirm the enclosure, slot, and serial number against the management console. We must also verify the replacement model and supported procedure.

5
00:00:40,920 --> 00:00:50,112
A: I will add the console evidence to the hardware ticket. Are there any other failing disks or warnings that would change the replacement risk?

6
00:00:50,712 --> 00:01:02,112
C: There are no additional failures reported, but I am checking error trends. I will also confirm the latest verified backup before authorizing the replacement.

7
00:01:02,712 --> 00:01:13,488
B: The spare matches the required model and capacity. I can have a second technician verify the physical labels and follow the approved replacement checklist.

8
00:01:14,088 --> 00:01:24,672
A: Please record both verifications in the ticket. Once replacement begins, who will monitor rebuild progress and watch for application performance impact?

9
00:01:25,272 --> 00:01:36,888
C: I own rebuild monitoring. Rebuild activity may increase storage latency, so we will track array health together with application response time and errors.

10
00:01:37,488 --> 00:01:46,152
B: Should we tell the business team a fixed completion time? They are asking when the service will have its normal protection level again.

11
00:01:46,752 --> 00:01:58,752
C: Not yet. The controller estimate can change with workload and disk performance. I will share the initial estimate as provisional after rebuild starts.

12
00:01:59,352 --> 00:02:11,904
A: I will coordinate the first status check at 14:00 UTC. We should distinguish service availability from restored redundancy in every update until the rebuild completes.

13
00:02:12,504 --> 00:02:24,960
B: Understood. We will proceed only after your checks and authorization are recorded. I own the physical replacement and will report any unexpected indication immediately.
